session: ta-0.9-epics-filed

## What changed (2026-07-29)

Filed six GitHub issues on `llm-d/llm-d-workload-variant-autoscaler` organizing the 0.9
(and carried-forward 0.8) analyzer / optimizer / observability work into epics. All labeled
`triage/accepted` + `release/v0.9`; `needs-triage` auto-stamp removed. Children assigned to
deanlorenz; epics unassigned (Epic D deliberately NOT assigned to shuynh2017).

New issues:
- **#1492** — [Epic] Multi-analyzer pipeline: pluggable analyzers feeding one optimizer *(new epic; prior art #408 closed)*
- **#1493** — [Epic] P/D-aware optimizer: role capacity aggregation & paired allocation *(new epic)*
- **#1494** — [Epic] WVA observability: scaling-decision visibility (metrics, logs, alerts) *(new epic; successor to closed #911)*
- **#1495** — engine: analyzer participation is opt-in *(child of #1492; fixed by PR #1479, merged)*
- **#1496** — engine: gate scale-down veto on per-analyzer liveness *(child of #1492; tracked by PR #1481, open)*
- **#1497** — engine: warn when runtime ConfigMap analyzer-enable requires a controller restart *(child of #1492; planned "PR E", no PR yet)*

Epic **B = existing #1005** (ThroughputAnalyzer) — adopted, not re-filed. Its 0.9 children
(#1480, #1478) were NOT filed as separate issues this pass ("new epics only" per Dean).
Shipped-0.8 children (#1225/#1228/#1246/#1266 under A; #1237/#1036/#994 under C; #1318/#1328/#1190
under D) are recorded as checklists in the epic bodies, not as retro issues (decision 4).
No trackers filed for any other-author work (A7 #1442, C1 #1237, D2 #1328, excluded bug fixes) —
Dean alerts those authors directly.

